<title>PERU: Peru says 1996 tax revenues up 4.9 percent.</title>
<headline>Peru says 1996 tax revenues up 4.9 percent.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's tax revenues rose 4.9 percent in real terms during 1996 to 19.94 billion soles, the National Superintendency of Tax Administration (SUNAT) said Thursday.</p>
<p>The SUNAT added that revenues in December were down 5.1 percent in real terms to 1.83 billion soles compared with the same month of 1995.</p>
<p>Peru's cumulative consumer inflation in the last 12 months of 1996 was 11.84 percent.</p>
<p>((-- Andrew Cawthorne, Lima newsroom, 511 221-2134))</p>
